[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. Quality assurance organization

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-003-MILUAV
TITLE: QA Organization
STATEMENT: Quality assurance organization includes QA manager, QA engineers, independent test team, and quality control personnel with defined roles and responsibilities.
RATIONALE: QA organization ensures effective quality assurance.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-004-MILUAV
TITLE: QA Independence
STATEMENT: Quality assurance activities shall be independent of development activities with separate reporting structure and authority for military software development.
RATIONALE: QA independence ensures objective quality assessment.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-005-MILUAV
TITLE: QA Authority
STATEMENT: Quality assurance shall have authority to stop development, testing, or deployment activities when quality standards are not met for military systems.
RATIONALE: QA authority ensures quality standards enforcement.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4. Quality assurance activities

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-006-MILUAV
TITLE: Process Audits
STATEMENT: Process audits include development process audits, testing process audits, and configuration management audits with compliance verification for military standards.
RATIONALE: Process audits ensure process compliance and effectiveness.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-007-MILUAV
TITLE: Product Audits
STATEMENT: Product audits include requirements audits, design audits, code audits, and test audits with quality verification for military software.
RATIONALE: Product audits ensure product quality and compliance.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-008-MILUAV
TITLE: Quality Reviews
STATEMENT: Quality reviews include peer reviews, technical reviews, and management reviews with documented findings and corrective actions.
RATIONALE: Quality reviews ensure early defect detection and correction.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-009-MILUAV
TITLE: Quality Testing
STATEMENT: Quality testing includes unit testing, integration testing, system testing, and acceptance testing with quality metrics and defect tracking.
RATIONALE: Quality testing ensures system reliability and performance.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5. Quality metrics

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-010-MILUAV
TITLE: Defect Metrics
STATEMENT: Defect metrics include defect density, defect severity, defect resolution time, and defect trends with automated tracking and reporting.
RATIONALE: Defect metrics ensure quality measurement and improvement.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-011-MILUAV
TITLE: Process Metrics
STATEMENT: Process metrics include development productivity, test coverage, requirement stability, and schedule adherence with performance tracking.
RATIONALE: Process metrics ensure process effectiveness and efficiency.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-012-MILUAV
TITLE: Product Metrics
STATEMENT: Product metrics include code complexity, performance benchmarks, security compliance, and reliability measures for military software.
RATIONALE: Product metrics ensure product quality and performance.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 6. Quality standards

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-013-MILUAV
TITLE: Military Standards
STATEMENT: Quality standards shall comply with MIL-STD-498, MIL-STD-882, and other applicable military standards for software development and testing.
RATIONALE: Military standards ensure compliance and interoperability.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-014-MILUAV
TITLE: Industry Standards
STATEMENT: Quality standards shall follow industry best practices including IEEE, ISO, and SEI CMMI standards for software quality assurance.
RATIONALE: Industry standards ensure quality best practices.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 7. Notes

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SQAP-015-MILUAV
TITLE: Continuous Improvement
STATEMENT: Quality assurance shall include continuous improvement processes with lessons learned, best practices, and process optimization for military software development.
RATIONALE: Continuous improvement ensures quality enhancement and efficiency.

[[/SECTION]] 